#: PART1.md:1
msgid "Part 1: Characterize the free-energy landscape with 2D Metadynamics"
msgstr "Part 1：2次元 Metadynamics による自由エネルギー地形の評価"

#: PART1.md:3
msgid ""
"Our strategy will consist first in characterizing on a simple system "
"(diuridine) the rate-limiting step in Magnesium binding to the backbone "
"phosphate groups."
msgstr ""
"まず単純な系 (Diuridine) で、Magnesium が Backbone の Phosphate 基に結合する際の Rate-limiting"
" Step を特定します。"

#: PART1.md:5
msgid "Description of the approach"
msgstr "方法の説明"

#: PART1.md:7
msgid ""
"We make the assumption that the binding dynamics are well described by the "
"two following collective variables (CVs):"
msgstr "結合 Dynamics は、次の2つの Collective Variables (CVs) でよく記述できると仮定します。"

#: PART1.md:8
msgid ""
"Coordination number of Mg<sup>2+</sup> with water oxygen atoms "
"(O<sub>W</sub>)"
msgstr "水の酸素原子 (O<sub>W</sub>) に対する Mg<sup>2+</sup> の Coordination Number"

#: PART1.md:9
msgid ""
"Coordination number of Mg<sup>2+</sup> with free phosphate oxygen atoms "
"(O<sub>P</sub>)"
msgstr ""
"遊離 Phosphate Oxygen (O<sub>P</sub>) に対する Mg<sup>2+</sup> の Coordination "
"Number"

#: PART1.md:15
msgid ""
"[!NOTE] We could also simply use the distance between Mg<sup>2+</sup> and "
"the *closest* O<sub>P</sub>, but it turns out convenient to treat both "
"exchanging ligands in a similar way and has the additional advantage to "
"allow binding to multiple O<sub>P</sub> in complex RNA motifs."
msgstr ""
"[!NOTE] Mg<sup>2+</sup> と *最も近い* O<sub>P</sub> の距離を使うこともできますが、交換する両方の Ligand"
" を同様に扱う方が便利です。複雑な RNA Motif で複数の O<sub>P</sub> への結合を扱える利点もあります。"

#: PART1.md:18
msgid ""
"To be used as biasing CVs, the coordination numbers are defined as smooth "
"functions of the Mg—O<sub>x</sub> pairwise distances. More precisely:"
msgstr ""
"Bias を加える CV として使えるよう、Coordination Number を Mg—O<sub>x</sub> の Pairwise "
"Distance の滑らかな関数として定義します。具体的には、"

#: PART1.md:26
msgid ""
"where $s(r)$ is a switching function between 1 and 0. In the following we "
"will use a cosine switching function"
msgstr ""
"$s(r)$ は1と0の間で切り替わる Switching Function です。以下では Cosine Switching Function "
"を使います。"

#: PART1.md:40
msgid ""
"with parameters $d_0 = 0.18~\\text{nm}$ (to include with some margin the "
"Mg—O<sub>W</sub> and Mg—O<sub>P</sub> equilibrium distance in the first "
"shell, $r_\\text{eq} = 0.21~\\text{nm}$) and $r_0 = 0.24~\\text{nm}$ (to "
"reach the density peak of the second hydration shell)."
msgstr ""
"パラメータは $d_0 = 0.18~\\text{nm}$（第1 Shell の Mg—O<sub>W</sub> と "
"Mg—O<sub>P</sub> の平衡距離 $r_\\text{eq} = 0.21~\\text{nm}$ を余裕を持って含めるため）、$r_0 ="
" 0.24~\\text{nm}$（第2 Hydration Shell の密度 Peak に届くため）です。"

#: PART1.md:42
msgid ""
"[!NOTE] Since we are using a $d_0$ slightly below the equilibrium distance "
"in the first shell ($r_\\text{eq}$), we can rescale the final value by "
"$s(r_\\text{eq})^{-1} = 1.039661$ to recover \"nice\" integer values for the"
" coordination states."
msgstr ""
"[!NOTE] $d_0$ が第1 Shell の平衡距離 ($r_\\text{eq}$) より少し小さいため、最終値を "
"$s(r_\\text{eq})^{-1} = 1.039661$ 倍すれば、Coordination State "
"に対応する扱いやすい整数値に戻せます。"

#: PART1.md:45
msgid "Implementation"
msgstr "実装"

#: PART1.md:47
msgid "Simulation set-up"
msgstr "シミュレーションの設定"

#: PART1.md:51
msgid "We provide as input files:"
msgstr "次の入力ファイルを用意しています。"

#: PART1.md:52
msgid ""
"`input.gro`: equilibrated simulation box with a diuridine molecule and a "
"single Mg²⁺ ion in water"
msgstr "`input.gro`：水中の Diuridine 1分子と Mg²⁺ Ion 1個を含む平衡化済み Box"

#: PART1.md:53
msgid "`run.mdp`: GROMACS MD parameter file"
msgstr "`run.mdp`：GROMACS の MD パラメータファイル"

#: PART1.md:54
msgid "`topol.top`: Standalone GROMACS topology file"
msgstr "`topol.top`：単独で使える GROMACS Topology"

#: PART1.md:56
msgid "[They can be downloaded here.](diuridine/diuridine.zip)"
msgstr "[こちらからダウンロードできます。](diuridine/diuridine.zip)"

#: PART1.md:58
msgid ""
"[!NOTE] The simulation box has one net positive charge that will be "
"compensated with a uniform background charge. This might lead to artifacts "
"which are likely irrelevant for our purpose here of estimating free-energy "
"barriers."
msgstr ""
"[!NOTE] Box の正味電荷は正の1で、一様な Background Charge により補償されます。Artifact "
"が生じる可能性はありますが、ここでの自由エネルギー Barrier の推定には影響しないと考えられます。"

#: PART1.md:61
msgid ""
"[!NOTE] The provided topology uses [*microMg* force field "
"parameters](https://github.com/bio-phys/optimizedMgFFs) from [Grotz *et al.*"
" (2021)](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.0c01281) [[1]](#references) for "
"Mg<sup>2+</sup>. It was parameterized to reproduce solvation free energy, "
"distance to oxygens in the first hydration shell, hydration number, activity"
" coefficient derivative in MgCl₂ solutions, and the binding affinity and "
"distance to the phosphate oxygens on nucleic acids."
msgstr ""
"[!NOTE] 付属の Topology は、Mg<sup>2+</sup> に [Grotz ら "
"(2021)](https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.0c01281) [[1]](#references) の "
"[*microMg* Force Field パラメータ](https://github.com/bio-phys/optimizedMgFFs) "
"を使います。Solvation 自由エネルギー、第1 Hydration Shell の酸素との距離、Hydration Number、MgCl₂ "
"溶液の Activity Coefficient の微分、核酸の Phosphate Oxygen への結合親和性と距離を再現するよう調整されています。"

#: PART1.md:64
msgid ""
"For now we can just preprocess the input files (`-maxwarn 1` is needed for "
"the non-zero total charge):"
msgstr "まず入力を前処理します（全電荷が0でないため `-maxwarn 1` が必要です）。"

#: PART1.md:70 PART1.md:147
msgid "Instructions"
msgstr "演習の手順"

#: PART1.md:72
msgid ""
"In a new file `plumed_metad.dat`, declare the atom groups that will be used "
"in CVs. You will need one for the Mg<sup>2+</sup>, one for the free "
"phosphate oxygen atoms (O1P/O2P in the GRO file), and one for all the water "
"oxygen atoms (OW)."
msgstr ""
"新しい `plumed_metad.dat` に、CV で使う原子 Group を宣言します。Mg<sup>2+</sup>、遊離 Phosphate "
"Oxygen（GRO 内の O1P/O2P）、すべての水の酸素 (OW) の Group が必要です。"

#: PART1.md:74
msgid ""
"[!TIP] When working with GROMACS, an easy way is to use an `index.ndx` file."
" This limits errors and increase legibility when specifying large atom "
"groups."
msgstr ""
"[!TIP] GROMACS では `index.ndx` を使うと簡単です。大きな原子 Group の指定ミスを減らし、読みやすくできます。"

#: PART1.md:79
msgid "To create a group for water oxygen atoms:"
msgstr "水の酸素原子の Group を作るには、"

#: PART1.md:83
msgid ""
"Finally we can rename this group for clarity, then save the index file:"
msgstr "最後に、わかりやすい名前に変更して Index ファイルを保存します。"

#: PART1.md:88
msgid "To use in a PLUMED file:"
msgstr "PLUMED 入力では、次のように使います。"

#: PART1.md:92
msgid ""
"Another way is to use the "
"[```MOLINFO```](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_m_o_l_i_n_f_o.html) selection features."
msgstr ""
"[```MOLINFO```](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_m_o_l_i_n_f_o.html) の選択機能を使う方法もあります。"

#: PART1.md:94
msgid ""
"Declare a CV for Mg<sup>2+</sup> coordination number with non-bridging "
"phosphate oxygens using the "
"[`COORDINATION`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_c_o_o_r_d_i_n_a_t_i_o_n.html) action. As explained "
"[above](#description-of-the-approach), will use a `COSINE` [switching "
"function](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/switchingfunction.html). However, free to experiment with other "
"possibilities!"
msgstr ""
"[`COORDINATION`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_c_o_o_r_d_i_n_a_t_i_o_n.html) で、Non-bridging Phosphate Oxygen に対する"
" Mg<sup>2+</sup> の Coordination Number CV を宣言してください。[上記](#description-of-"
"the-approach) のとおり `COSINE` [Switching "
"Function](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/switchingfunction.html) を使いますが、ほかの選択肢も自由に試してください。"

#: PART1.md:96
msgid ""
"Similarly, declare a CV for Mg<sup>2+</sup> coordination number with "
"O<sub>W</sub> using the "
"[`COORDINATION`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_c_o_o_r_d_i_n_a_t_i_o_n.html) action."
msgstr ""
"同様に、[`COORDINATION`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_c_o_o_r_d_i_n_a_t_i_o_n.html) で O<sub>W</sub> に対する Mg<sup>2+</sup>"
" の Coordination Number CV を宣言します。"

#: PART1.md:98
msgid ""
"Declare a (well-tempered) Metadynamics bias on the two CVs with "
"[`METAD`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html)."
msgstr ""
"[`METAD`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-doc/html/_m_e_t_a_d.html) "
"で2つの CV に Well-tempered Metadynamics の Bias を宣言します。"

#: PART1.md:99
msgid ""
"[!NOTE] The choice of the Gaussian widths is an important parameter. Chosing"
" a too large $\\sigma$ can oversmooth the underlying free-energy landscape, "
"while a too small $\\sigma$ will dramatically increase convergence time. A "
"good rule of thumb is to take $\\sigma$ on the scale of the smallest "
"features you expect to resolve along the CV. We suggest $\\sigma = 0.05$ for"
" the coordination CV."
msgstr ""
"[!NOTE] Gaussian の幅は重要です。$\\sigma$ が大きすぎると自由エネルギー地形を過剰に平滑化し、$\\sigma$ "
"が小さすぎると収束時間が大幅に増えます。CV に沿って解像したい最小の特徴と同程度の $\\sigma$ を選ぶのが目安です。Coordination "
"CV には $\\sigma = 0.05$ を推奨します。"

#: PART1.md:102
msgid ""
"The metadynamics will encourage the system to explore the whole range of "
"accessible coordination numbers. To avoid exploring a priori irrelevant "
"areas of the configuration space and accelerate convergence we will add "
"semiharmonic potential walls. Use "
"[`LOWER_WALLS`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_l_o_w_e_r__w_a_l_l_s.html) and "
"[`UPPER_WALLS`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_u_p_p_e_r__w_a_l_l_s.html) to restrain the O<sub>W</sub> "
"coordination CV between $4$ and $7$."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics は、到達可能な Coordination Number の全範囲を探索するよう促します。関係がないとわかっている "
"Configuration 空間の探索を避け、収束を速めるため、Semiharmonic Potential Wall "
"を加えます。[`LOWER_WALLS`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_l_o_w_e_r__w_a_l_l_s.html) と "
"[`UPPER_WALLS`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/_u_p_p_e_r__w_a_l_l_s.html) で O<sub>W</sub> Coordination CV を "
"$4$〜$7$ に制限してください。"

