msgstr "GPU で加速した Node では数時間かかり、約4 Gb のデータが生成されます。"

#: PART1.md:143
msgid "Analysis"
msgstr "解析"

#: PART1.md:145
msgid ""
"Once the simulation is completed, we can analyze the free-energy landscape "
"on the selected CV-space. One way of doing that is to trust the summed "
"Gaussian hills as the opposite of the converged free-energy landscape. A "
"somewhat more precise (yet simple) way is to reweight the entire trajectory "
"assuming it was generated with the final metadynamics bias [[2, "
"3]](#references)."
msgstr ""
"終了後、選んだ CV 空間の自由エネルギー地形を解析します。1つの方法は、足し合わせた Gaussian Hill "
"の符号反転を収束した自由エネルギー地形とみなすことです。もう少し正確で簡単な方法は、最終的な Metadynamics Bias "
"で生成されたと仮定して全 Trajectory を Reweighting することです [[2, 3]](#references)。"

#: PART1.md:149
msgid ""
"Using [`plumed sum_hills`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/sum_hills.html), extract the free-energy surface (FES) from the "
"accumulated gaussians stored in the `HILLS` file."
msgstr ""
"[`plumed sum_hills`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/sum_hills.html) で、`HILLS` に蓄積した Gaussian から自由エネルギー表面 (FES) "
"を抽出してください。"

#: PART1.md:151
msgid ""
"Using [`plumed driver`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/driver.html), recompute the instantaneous value of the metadynamics"
" bias for every trajectory frame, restarting from the final `HILLS` file."
msgstr ""
"最終的な `HILLS` から再開し、[`plumed driver`](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.9/user-"
"doc/html/driver.html) で各 Trajectory Frame の Metadynamics Bias "
"の瞬時値を再計算してください。"

#: PART1.md:153
msgid ""
"[!TIP] You will need a new plumed input file (you can call it "
"`plumed_static.dat`) identical to the previous one but with the following "
"modifications:"
msgstr "[!TIP] 前の入力と同じ新しい plumed 入力（`plumed_static.dat` など）を用意し、次のように変更します。"

#: PART1.md:155
msgid "`METAD` component should contain the `RESTART=YES` option"
msgstr "`METAD` に `RESTART=YES` を指定する。"

#: PART1.md:156
msgid ""
"To avoid modifying the `HILLS` file, set the `HEIGHT` parameter to 0 and the"
" `PACE` to a large number (e.g. 10⁹)"
msgstr "`HILLS` を変更しないよう、`HEIGHT` を0、`PACE` を大きな数（例えば10⁹）にする。"

