"![Metadynamics timeseries figure](solutions/figures/metad_timeseries.png)"
msgstr "![Metadynamics の時系列](solutions/figures/metad_timeseries.png)"

#: PART1.md:169
msgid ""
"![Metadynamics free-energy surface figure](solutions/figures/metad_fes.png)"
msgstr "![Metadynamics の自由エネルギー表面](solutions/figures/metad_fes.png)"

#: PART1.md:171
msgid ""
"[!NOTE] On these plots, the raw values for $n_\\mathrm{O_P}$ and "
"$n_\\mathrm{O_W}$ have been [scaled to integral values](#description-of-the-"
"approach)."
msgstr ""
"[!NOTE] 図の $n_\\mathrm{O_P}$ と $n_\\mathrm{O_W}$ は、元の値を "
"[整数値にスケール](#description-of-the-approach) しています。"

#: PART1.md:174
msgid ""
"We can see that the metadynamics covered most of the space within the "
"restraints. The reweighting overall agrees with the summed hills FES but "
"resolves better sharp features that are otherwise smoothed by the chosen "
"Gaussian $\\sigma$-value. The deep band on the left (at $n_\\mathrm{O_P} = "
"0$) is the unbound state. A pre-bound (or outer-sphere bound) state is "
"visible for $n_\\mathrm{O_W} \\approx 6$ and small non-zero values of "
"$n_\\mathrm{O_P}$, and is separated from the bound state ($n_\\mathrm{O_W} "
"\\approx 5$ and $n_\\mathrm{O_P} \\approx 1$) by a minimum free-energy path "
"whose saddle point is located around a 7-coordinated transition state "
"($n_\\mathrm{O_W} \\approx 6$, $n_\\mathrm{O_P} \\approx 1$). This "
"corresponds to an associative interchange (*I<sub>a</sub>*) mechanism "
"already observed for this force-field [[4]](#references)."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics が拘束内の大部分の空間を探索したことがわかります。Reweighting は Hill の和からの FES "
"と全体的に一致し、Gaussian の $\\sigma$ により平滑化される鋭い特徴も、よりよく解像します。左側の深い帯 "
"($n_\\mathrm{O_P} = 0$) は非結合状態です。$n_\\mathrm{O_W} \\approx "
"6$、$n_\\mathrm{O_P}$ が小さな非0値の領域には Pre-bound（Outer-sphere Bound）状態があります。結合状態 "
"($n_\\mathrm{O_W} \\approx 5$、$n_\\mathrm{O_P} \\approx 1$) との間の Minimum "
"Free Energy Path は、7配位 Transition State ($n_\\mathrm{O_W} \\approx "
"6$、$n_\\mathrm{O_P} \\approx 1$) 付近に Saddle Point を持ちます。この Force Field "
"で既に観測された Associative Interchange (*I<sub>a</sub>*) 機構に対応します "
"[[4]](#references)。"

#: PART1.md:176
msgid ""
"[!NOTE] The experimentally suggested mechanism is an interchange "
"dissociative one (*I<sub>d</sub>*), suggesting that the observed associative"
" pathway is an artifact of the particular force field we use."
msgstr ""
"[!NOTE] 実験で示唆されるのは Interchange Dissociative (*I<sub>d</sub>*) 機構なので、観測された "
"Associative Pathway は、この Force Field に由来する Artifact と考えられます。"

#: PART1.md:179
msgid ""
"The [next section](PART2.md) of the tutorial will focus on exploiting this "
"data to design a bias that reduces the free-energy barrier while minimally "
"affecting the remaining part of the FES."
msgstr ""
"[次の節](PART2.md) では、このデータを使い、FES のほかの部分への影響を最小限に抑えて自由エネルギー Barrier を下げる Bias "
"を設計します。"

